{"id": "unknown-2026-08-26-005", "date": "2026-08-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Moody’s affirms Philippines’ ‘Baa2’ credit rating, stable outlook", "content": "Moody’s Ratings has affirmed the Philippines’ ‘Baa2’ investment-grade rating and maintained its stable outlook, holding the country’s credit standing steady even as the latter navigates rising energy costs and a public infrastructure spending slowdown. \nIt expects fiscal metrics to stabilise over two years, backed by a recovery in growth and the government’s continued commitment to fiscal consolidation. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/moody-s-affirms-philippines-baa2-credit-rating-stable-outlook-312953-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
