{"id": "unknown-2026-08-26-007", "date": "2026-08-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "$3.1 bn lost; inside the shift at 30 US fashion companies", "content": "TexPro shows US HS 61 and HS 62 imports fell 7.77 per cent year on year to about $36.90 billion in January-June 2026.\nChina and India lost nearly $2.98 billion, while gains by Vietnam, Cambodia and Indonesia totalled only about $407 million.\nUSFIA respondents sourced from 49 countries, but 47.4 per cent expect to use fewer suppliers as tariff risk reshapes sourcing.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/-3-1-bn-lost-inside-the-shift-at-30-us-fashion-companies-312934-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
